				<h1>The Memory Of Trees (1995)</h1>
                
<a class="new-amazon-album-link" href="https://amzn.to/499iOEx" rel="nofollow sponsored noopener" target="_blank">
    <Image src={tmot} alt="The Memory Of Trees (1995)" width="300" height="300" />
</a>

<p><strong><em>The Memory Of Trees</em></strong> is the fourth studio album by Irish singer and composer <strong>Enya</strong>, released on <strong>20 November 1995</strong> by <strong>WEA Records</strong> in the United Kingdom and <strong>5 December 1995</strong> by <strong>Reprise Records</strong> in the United States.</p>

<p>The album won Enya her second <strong>Grammy Award</strong> for <strong>Best New Age Album</strong> in <strong>1997</strong>.</p>

<p><a href="https://amzn.to/499iOEx" rel="nofollow sponsored noopener" target="_blank">Stream or download Enya songs</a></p>

<h3>Recording and Production</h3>

<p>Recording took place between <strong>1993 and 1995</strong> at the newly rebuilt <strong>Aigle Studio</strong> in <strong>Killiney, County Dublin</strong>.</p>

<p>It was Enya's first album recorded entirely in Ireland and her first studio release without any guest musicians.</p>

<p>Enya composed all music, sang all vocal parts, and played all instruments, including piano, synthesizers, violin, cello, and percussion.</p>

<h3>Artwork and Visual Inspirations</h3>
    
<p>Its cover art was adapted from a 1906 painting titled <a href="MaxfieldParrish_YoungKing.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">"The Young King of the Black Isles"</a> by <strong>Maxfield Parrish</strong>.</p>

<p>Enya poses as the young king in a costume designed by <strong>Elizabeth Emanuel</strong>, with layout by <strong>Sooky Choi</strong>.</p>

<h3>Themes and Lore</h3>

<p>The album explores themes of <strong>Irish and Druid mythology</strong>, journeys, home, religion, dreams, and love, with lyrics performed in <strong>English</strong>, <strong>Irish</strong>, <strong>Latin</strong>, and <strong>Spanish</strong>.</p>

<p>As <a href="/roma-ryan-nicky/">Roma Ryan</a>, Enya's lyricist, remarks in the liner notes of the <a href="#The_Memory_Of_Trees">The Memory Of Trees</a> song for the later collection <a href="/paint-the-sky-with-stars/"><em>Paint The Sky With Stars</em></a>:</p>

<blockquote>
    <p>"In ancient Celtic belief trees had spirits within them and were considered sacred. They were the keepers of memory and lore."</p>
    <p>"The future we look at may give us another interpretation of the title, with the destruction of the world's rainforests it may turn out to be that the memory of trees is nothing more than that for us - a memory."</p>
</blockquote>

